1
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,320
*trembling breaths*

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,600
Krajewski, Franz, Corporal.

3
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:29,480
Buried alive on the Somme,
October 8th, admitted on the 16th.

4
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:32,439
(Forster) What civilian position
did you hold before the war?

5
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:37,240
*Krajewski stutters*
Policeman, Staff Surgeon, sir.

6
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,360
Well, let's see
if we can get you back on your feet.

7
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:41,520
At your command.

8
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,480
*occasional coughing*

9
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:47,400
Rath, Anno, Assistant Doctor,
buried alive on the Western Front.

10
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,440
A medical man, yes?

11
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:53,920
Yes, Staff Surgeon, sir.
- With whom did you study?

12
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,720
Professor Schmidt.

13
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,640
Which Schmidt?

14
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:02,040
Professor Ferdinand August Schmidt,
Bonn University, Staff Surgeon, sir.

15
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,680
Sports Schmidt.
*Rath nods*

16
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,160
Yes.

17
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,360
You won't be making a surgeon anymore.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,840
Suggestive therapy.
- (Hildegard) Monday, six o'clock.

19
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,960
And who do we have here?

20
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:18,320
Hitler, Adolf, Lance Corporal,

21
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,040
corneal burn from gas attack.

22
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,800
Corneal burns in our psychiatric ward?

23
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,280
(Hildegard) The ophthalmologist
could find no chemical burns.

24
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,680
Let me see.

25
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,080
*patient coughs and clears throat*

26
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,160
Chemical burns?

27
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,800
Yes, Staff Surgeon, sir. Yellow Cross mustard gas.

28
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:51,000
(Patient) You're just malingering.
- (Strelow) Rear-echelon bastard.

29
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,920
You've really had a rough go of it,
Lance Corporal.

30
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,360
Thank you, Professor, sir.

31
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,400
(Forster) And here?

32
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,520
(Hildegard) Kasabian, Edgar.
Sergeant. Doesn't speak anymore.

33
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:04,240
A mute.

34
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,320
And?

35
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,480
Wosniak, Karl, Private,

36
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,280
shrapnel impact, left temple, insomnia.

37
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:25,200
Consultation.
First thing tomorrow morning with the colleagues.

38
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,280
(Hildegard) Right away, Doctor.

39
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,760
Strelow, Paul, demolition specialist,

40
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,920
shrapnel wounds
and somatoform pain disorder.

41
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,480
*bells tolling*

42
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,400
*eerie music*

43
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,560
*rhythmic music*

44
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:39,960
*quiet murmuring*

45
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:42,640
*water splashing*

46
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,440
*suspenseful pulsing music*

47
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,000
Have you seen Wosniak?

48
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:54,480
Who?

49
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,000
Karl Wosniak.

50
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,480
*bearded man mumbles*

51
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,960
*music builds slowly*

52
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,920
There he sleeps.

53
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,360
Karl?

54
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,440
Wosniak, you old scoundrel.

55
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,400
Get up, soup's ready.

56
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,440
*music fades out*

57
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,760
*mysterious music*

58
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,520
*traffic noise*

59
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:55,320
*snoring, coughing*

60
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,760
*music fades out*

61
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:26,200
You've been drinking.
That is forbidden here.

62
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:30,040
Mind your own business.

63
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:34,880
(Böhm) Who are you anyway?
I've never seen you here before.

64
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,800
I am Marinus van der Lubbe.

65
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,760
I can get you something to drink.

66
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,800
I can get anything.
You can have Genever.

67
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,560
Not watered-down grain booze
like that over there.

68
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,320
Leave me in peace.

69
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,920
*Böhm vomits*

70
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,600
*Böhm coughs*

71
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,840
Want a taste?

72
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,120
*gentle music*

73
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,600
You're welcome.

74
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,440
*men speaking indistinctly*

75
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:26,640
(Grundmann) I have no idea
what gave you the impression

76
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:29,560
that I was authorized
to hand over patient records to you.

77
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:33,720
I hold an official order
entitling me to inspect records.

78
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,320
No, young lady,

79
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:40,760
these patient files may only
be inspected by a physician,

80
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,720
and even then, only
in justified exceptional cases.

81
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:46,440
A homicide investigation
is an exceptional case.

82
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:47,520
That may well be.

83
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:50,840
However, it must be ordered
by a court of law.

84
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:54,560
I am without doubt far better versed
in statutory law than you.

85
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:55,640
Is that so?

86
00:06:57,480 --> 00:07:00,680
The medical file of the Reich Chancellor
is, moreover,

87
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:02,800
a politically sensitive document.

88
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,000
I doubt you will find a judge

89
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,880
who would legitimize your request.

90
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:27,000
Yet you could confirm
the existence of a file for me, couldn't you?

91
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,520
Not personally, no.

92
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,360
However, there is, of course,
a central register for that.

93
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,600
And would you be so kind
as to check it for me?

94
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,760
As a courtesy.

95
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,200
Pardon me?

96
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,360
*curious music*

97
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:52,040
*distant rumbling*

98
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,880
Right then, here it is.

99
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:09,040
(whispers) Medical file
of Lance Corporal Adolf Hitler.

100
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:12,240
If I am reading this correctly,
this file comprises 21 pages

101
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,720
and was checked out only three times,
correct?

102
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,360
Good heavens.

103
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:19,040
I worked in the archives
during my basic training.

104
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:20,800
Why, that makes us almost colleagues.

105
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,840
You wouldn't mind if I noted down
the names of the borrowers?

106
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,240
Not at all, go right ahead.

107
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,920
Thank you.

108
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:33,679
'Friedrich-Wilhelms-Universität
Berlin, doctoral dissertation.'

109
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,919
Twice by the same person?

110
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:38,720
Signature illegible,
and after that...

111
00:08:39,159 --> 00:08:40,159
Curious.

112
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,360
Excuse me?

113
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,440
Look at this.

114
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:49,000
'Munich Public Prosecutor's Office,
checked out on November 20th, 1924.'

115
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,600
Truly unbelievable.

116
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:54,520
'Prosecutor M. Dresse.'

117
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,640
Well, the fellow has quite some nerve.

118
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,520
They never returned the file.

119
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,360
Prosecutor Dresse.

120
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,600
In black and white. Nine years.

121
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,120
This index card is evidence.
I must confiscate it.

122
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,240
I will sign a receipt for it,
and we will follow up on the matter.

123
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,360
As will we.

124
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,600
Such sloppiness must be brought to light.

125
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,680
Indeed.

126
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,120
(Jacoby) You are listening to a live broadcast

127
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:24,240
from the memorial service
at Berlin Cathedral

128
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:28,040
in honor of the deceased
SA man, Paul Strelow.

129
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,720
Hundreds of thousands of Berlin citizens
line the streets of the city.

130
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:35,200
The funeral procession is now getting underway

131
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,440
towards the Invaliden Cemetery.

132
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:42,440
High-ranking government officials
are attending the burial.

133
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:46,320
Do you plan on listening to that
the whole time, Frau Elisabeth?

134
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:48,520
I'll listen to it until I can believe it.

135
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:51,040
And so far,
that is not yet the case.

136
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,760
If this continues between you
and that wireless radio,

137
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:56,200
I will have to call
a vote of confidence.

138
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:58,080
Either that box or me.

139
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,760
*music from radio*

140
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,160
Well.
*he clears his throat*

141
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:07,240
Has Herr Heymann turned up yet?

142
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:09,880
No.
- Watch your step.

143
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,840
They have their eyes on you.

144
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,040
Right, I must hurry off
to the Reichstag.

145
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:18,760
Your humble servant.

146
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,840
Best of luck.

147
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:24,040
...of the comrades and the leader
of his followers.

148
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,760
*bells tolling*

149
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:32,320
(von Levetzow)
Good morning, gentlemen.

150
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,720
Herr Police President.

151
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:35,760
I have just arrived from the state funeral

152
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:38,480
for SA man Strelow
and Patrolman Hoffmann.

153
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:40,600
Goebbels delivered the eulogy,

154
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,960
and the Führer himself
was personally present.

155
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,720
You see the importance

156
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:46,840
the party leadership attaches
to the Strelow case.

157
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,400
The case is in my department.

158
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,840
The party leadership can count
on our thorough work.

159
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,360
Fully and completely.

160
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,600
That is good.

161
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:58,320
Minister Göring has entrusted this to me.
Here you are.

162
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,200
(Wendt) What is this exactly?
- A list

163
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:07,200
of enemies of the national uprising
to be interned.

164
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:09,600
Nearly 10,000 in Berlin alone.

165
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,640
That exceeds even our capacities.

166
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,680
Arrest the first hundred,

167
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:19,400
and select a credible number
of suspects

168
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,640
for the murder of Strelow.

169
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:23,040
A signal has been demanded by leadership.

170
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:27,640
A signal we shall send.
Gentlemen.

171
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
*door closes*

172
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,240
Herr Government Councillor,

173
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:33,840
the Strelow case
is no longer with us.

174
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,920
Excuse me?

175
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:37,160
It was handed back to Homicide.

176
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:42,200
*somber music*

177
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:46,280
Mhm.

178
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:49,320
*phone ringing
from adjoining room*

179
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:54,160
The same winding.
*he huffs*

180
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:00,200
*background conversations*

181
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:05,240
During the last roundup...

182
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:09,840
(Secretary) Herr Krajewski,
please follow me.

183
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,680
Yes.

184
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:19,880
Come on in.

185
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,160
(Krajewski) Thank you.
- Please.

186
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:28,800
I had you brought in because you found this...

187
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,240
this vagrant.

188
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:33,840
Yes,
one of my former comrades.

189
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,920
Is that so?

190
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,120
Wosniak, Karl, correct?
- Yes.

191
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,400
Soldier of the 34th

192
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,760
Corps of the Bavarian Guard.

193
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,040
We were at the front together.

194
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:48,920
Well.

195
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,280
Wosniak isn't the only one.

196
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:55,520
First Lieutenant Huber disappears
in Augsburg,

197
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:58,560
and now here in the capital, Strelow.

198
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:02,040
Buried with a state funeral.

199
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,120
Strelow, you say?

200
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,600
Paul Strelow?

201
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,040
Yes.

202
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:13,600
How do you know all these men?
- We are veterans.

203
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,280
*stutters* War-disabled.

204
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,080
Shared history.

205
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,720
*laughter in next room*

206
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,320
Hey.

207
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,720
*Böhm knocks*

208
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,920
What is your name?
- Krajewski, Franz.

209
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,440
I don't want to be next.

210
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:40,480
*dark music*

211
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,640
Protect me.

212
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:46,280
Please.
- *knocking*

213
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,680
Excuse the interruption.

214
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:49,920
Government Councillor Wendt

215
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,920
and Chief Inspector Gennat
wish to speak with you.

216
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Right now?

217
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,000
Immediately, yes.

218
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,400
*Böhm sighs*

219
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:00,960
Wait here.

220
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,080
(Wendt) Make no mistake about it,

221
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,760
the case must be handled
by the proper department.

222
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:23,400
It is being handled there. With us.

223
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,840
We are dealing with two murders

224
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:29,560
at a single crime scene
with two different murder weapons,

225
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,600
and most likely two different killers.

226
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,520
And sitting over there is a witness
who testifies

227
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,640
that the Strelow case
is part of an entire serial killing.

228
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:40,000
Yet the primary motive is political,

229
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,080
and thus jurisdiction is indisputable.

230
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:45,320
Because you want to exploit the case
for your own agenda.

231
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,880
Would you care to repeat that,
Chief Detective?

232
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,200
You heard me.

233
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:56,120
You allow your subordinates
to speak to you like that?

234
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,200
Your case, Councillor.

235
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:02,600
Chief Inspector, I beg of you...
- Thank you, colleague Böhm.

236
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:03,760
You heard me.

237
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:06,480
Turn over all files
to the Government Councillor.

238
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,280
(Wendt) Thank you, Chief Inspector.

239
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,520
You take charge of this.

240
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,080
*tense music*

241
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,800
(Sebald) Where is
your star witness, then?

242
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:32,440
Where is the man
who was sitting right here a moment ago?

243
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,760
There, take it.
Now you have everything.

244
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:47,800
Thank you.
- Truly unbelievable.

245
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,400
Ridiculous.

246
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:01,920
Your name?
- Squad Leader Kummer, Herr...

247
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,880
Senior Detective Sebald,
Political Police.

248
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,560
At your service,
Herr Senior Detective.

249
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:08,640
Have you ever made an arrest before?

250
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,960
No, Herr Senior Detective.

251
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,440
Then it's about time.

252
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,560
*music continues dynamically*

253
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:24,240
What's gotten into Böhm?

254
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,560
Political Police meddling.

255
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:33,120
Reinhold, I have something here.

256
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:35,560
Will you help me find
a doctoral dissertation?

257
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:37,440
The signature is hard to decipher.

258
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:40,160
Search, yes. Read, no.

259
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,480
You're a darling.

260
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,800
*excited clamor of voices*

261
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:58,120
Ladies and gentlemen,
order!

262
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,640
Herr Reichstag President, please!

263
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,480
Order your faction to silence!

264
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:06,520
*indistinct shouting*

265
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:11,000
Please come to order!

266
00:17:14,599 --> 00:17:17,079
Ladies and gentlemen!

267
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,880
*voices quiet down*

268
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:24,359
Today, the new forces of government
have attempted

269
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:28,079
to shamelessly exploit a murder
for political gain.

270
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,960
*boos, applause*

271
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:35,320
We shall confront such dirty tricks
with the voice of the people and their will,

272
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:40,080
and we shall assemble.

273
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:44,560
Tomorrow at noon
between the Cathedral and the Palace.

274
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,400
And our numbers will be greater.

275
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:49,840
Far greater.

276
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:53,160
And we will demonstrate to the world

277
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,960
that the majority of Berliners,

278
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,760
nay, the majority of all Germans...

279
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:00,040
Herr Chairman,

280
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,280
you are abusing parliament
for pure agitprop.

281
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,040
Such talk has no place
in this honorable house!

282
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,960
*agitated shouts*

283
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,280
(Chairman)
Such words from your lips,

284
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:14,360
Herr Reichstag President, are,
with all due respect, bitterest satire.

285
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,120
*applause*

286
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,280
Excuse me.

287
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,400
Well?

288
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:22,920
How are things with you?
- Wels has been talking non-stop.

289
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,760
Or whatever you want to call
that shrieking down there.

290
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:28,360
Have you heard anything from Heymann?
- Nothing.

291
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:30,440
Dozens were arrested yesterday.

292
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:32,200
Nobody knows where they're being taken.

293
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:35,600
These are facts that have nothing
to do with agitation,

294
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:38,160
facts that must be clarified publicly!

295
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:40,040
Deputy Wels, restrain yourself!

296
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:42,400
Or I will revoke your right to speak!

297
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,720
*applause*

298
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,960
Tomorrow at noon we shall see

299
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,520
who truly speaks with the voice of the people.

300
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:50,600
Bravo!

301
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:52,040
*uproar and shouting*

302
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,400
Who speaks with the voice of the people!

303
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,480
*indistinct calls*

304
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,320
*turmoil continues*

305
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,680
Ah, Deputy Thälmann.

306
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,040
*boos*

307
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,000
Glad you could find the time.

308
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,640
*indistinct shouts*

309
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,840
I know Wels, you can reason with the man.

310
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,200
The Communists seem like
the bigger challenge to me.

311
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,640
You might be right about that.

312
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,120
(Woman) Herr Reichstag President!

313
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:21,680
On behalf of the Social Democrats,
I move

314
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:25,720
for the expulsion of the National Socialist faction.

315
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:28,320
*roaring applause*

316
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:31,400
As well as that of the Communists!

317
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:36,120
Your conduct is unworthy
of this house!

318
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,200
Denied!

319
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:40,000
*indistinct roar of voices*

320
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,040
*arguments over the radio*

321
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:51,480
(Woman) Utterly disgraceful!
Inconceivable!

322
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:56,080
Orders from the director:
switch over, I'll take the mic.

323
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,440
Find something musical.
- Pardon?

324
00:19:58,520 --> 00:19:59,960
Luigi Bernauer.

325
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:02,000
*voices fall silent*

326
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:09,040
Dear listeners at your wireless receivers.

327
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:10,720
Unpredictability is

328
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:13,320
an inevitable companion
of our new medium.

329
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,080
We therefore ask you to pardon

330
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:17,280
any occasional interruptions.

331
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:21,320
There now follows a midday musical greeting
from our orchestra

332
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:23,680
to all Berliners.

333
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:25,800
Luigi Bernauer.

334
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,960
*"Ich möcht' ein Würstchen mit Senf beschmiert"
by Luigi Bernauer*

335
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,720
*cheerful music*

336
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:38,040
# I'd like a sausage smeared with mustard #

337
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:41,720
# I need something warm, I'm freezing cold #

338
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:45,880
# I'll gladly forgo a lover's kiss #

339
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:49,920
# I want a sausage, I want a dog! #

340
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,840
# I'd like a sausage smeared with mustard #

341
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:57,960
# I need something warm, I'm freezing cold #

342
00:20:58,040 --> 00:21:01,800
# I'll gladly forgo a lover's kiss #

343
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,840
# I want a sausage #

344
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,920
# I want a dog! #

345
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,560
Enjoy your meal.
- Enjoy your meal.

346
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:14,080
Well?
What does Forster's appointment book say?

347
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,000
We're checking out all the institutes

348
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:19,120
the doctor was connected with.

349
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,280
Here.

350
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:26,280
And?
- Mealtime. Nothing to report.

351
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:29,280
Do you have any idea how many dissertations
there were in 1923/24

352
00:21:29,360 --> 00:21:30,840
in the medical faculty?

353
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,160
*she shakes her head*
Countless.

354
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:36,120
So far, no match

355
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,200
with the signature on the index card.

356
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,720
On the upside, they even have potato cakes today.

357
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,880
Say what?
- Dätscher.

358
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,440
He means potato pancakes.

359
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:46,800
Ah, Reibekuchen.

360
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:49,960
Yes, magnificent. With applesauce.
- Did you see?

361
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,880
There are pancakes.

362
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,920
(Czerwinski) You won't believe
where I just was.

363
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,600
The world is colorful. Very colorful.

364
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:01,160
Straight from the Institute for Sexual Science.

365
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,240
Hirschfeld's place?

366
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:04,360
Quite a crowd there, let me tell you.

367
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:08,560
And that Dr. Forster is well known there.

368
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,440
Right, what'll it be?

369
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:14,480
*hesitates* The...
- The daily special at the top, please.

370
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,840
For everyone?
- Yes.

371
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,880
Four potato pancakes, coming right up.
- Very good.

372
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:20,840
What did Hirschfeld have to do with Forster?

373
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:24,520
He wrote expert evaluations
for Dr. Hirschfeld.

374
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,280
What kind of evaluations?

375
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:29,680
Psychological or psychiatric.
Mostly prior to reassignments.

376
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:32,120
(Henning) Reassignments?

377
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:34,040
(Czerwinski) Transformations or whatever.

378
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:36,160
Whenever something isn't quite right
with someone,

379
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:38,160
up in the belfry, I suppose.

380
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,920
Could you be a bit more specific?

381
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,400
This Dr. Forster, he...

382
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:45,760
wrote down assessments of his patients.

383
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,600
It's required by law.

384
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,800
So he acted as an expert witness
for the institute?

385
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:52,120
Yes, exactly. An expert.

386
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:54,520
(Czerwinski) Ah, here comes the food.

387
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,000
(Czerwinski) Thank you.
Thank you.

388
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,960
*clattering silverware*

389
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:09,160
No appetite?

390
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,360
*Gräf breathes heavily*

391
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,000
Reinhold, what...?

392
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,240
Professor Forster wrote...

393
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:27,800
expert reports for people
wishing to change their sex.

394
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:29,840
What?

395
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:32,680
How do you know that?

396
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:35,000
My name was in Forster's appointment book.

397
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:38,320
I had an appointment with him.

398
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:44,040
I saw him
and alerted the police.

399
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:48,800
And I tore the page
out of his calendar.

400
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:56,520
There, it's out.

401
00:23:58,320 --> 00:23:59,640
*she gasps in disbelief*

402
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,800
But why?

403
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:07,320
Professor Forster was supposed
to write an evaluation for me.

404
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:11,040
You want to...
I want to...

405
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:14,600
become a woman.

406
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,320
(Gräf) Yes.

407
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:24,000
And that's possible?

408
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:25,160
It is...

409
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:28,200
it's not without danger,
but it is possible.

410
00:24:28,360 --> 00:24:30,240
I personally know two women

411
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:32,960
who have lived that way for some time.

412
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:36,760
But why?

413
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:39,360
Charlotte,
you don't do something like this for fun,

414
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:42,560
or just so a dress fits better.

415
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:47,440
I want it so that I can go on living.

416
00:24:53,520 --> 00:24:55,680
Yes, now you know.

417
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:58,800
You can report me to the Buddha,
of course.

418
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,440
It's all ruined anyway.

419
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:04,680
Forster is gone, Hirschfeld's in Switzerland.

420
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:10,680
*gentle piano music*

421
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:14,320
Reinhold.

422
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:19,720
Nothing is ruined. Nothing at all.
Least of all for us.

423
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:23,920
And as for that stupid page, I think

424
00:25:25,520 --> 00:25:27,560
it can just stay missing.

425
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:30,680
Yes.

426
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:33,400
Precisely.

427
00:25:35,080 --> 00:25:38,000
(Henning) And we'll even keep searching for it.

428
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:41,680
(Czerwinski) Of course.
- (Henning) Naturally.

429
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:44,480
With the greatest zeal.
- Utmost dedication.

430
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:48,720
You know how it is:

431
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,600
if someone takes a swing at one of us...

432
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:58,920
*music fades out*

433
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:02,240
Gereon's father is Police President
of Cologne, after all.

434
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:05,160
Maybe you should simply
try reaching out to him.

435
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:07,680
At your command,
Herr Senior Detective.

436
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:12,160
What?

437
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,000
(Sebald) Where do our colleagues think
they're going?

438
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:15,560
Can't see how that's any of your business.

439
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:19,640
(Sebald) It is very much my business.

440
00:26:19,720 --> 00:26:22,760
There are arrests scheduled
which these officers will carry out.

441
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:25,120
By law, the auxiliary police units

442
00:26:25,200 --> 00:26:28,760
remain obliged to have sworn officers
accompany them during arrests.

443
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,680
You are those sworn officers.

444
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,880
He isn't our commanding officer.

445
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,960
Councillor Wendt is, however.

446
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:37,240
So let's move, as discussed.

447
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:40,040
Or should I report you
for refusal to obey orders?

448
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:44,080
Any day now?

449
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,760
(Langenberger) Let's go.
- Hey.

450
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:47,280
*dramatic music*

451
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:08,200
(Langenberger)
Here, number 32. Mandel, physician.

452
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:10,160
Two flights up, left side.

453
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:11,960
We're bringing the man out.

454
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,360
Understood?

455
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:14,480
*louder* Understood?

456
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,840
*Langenberger whistles*

457
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,440
*Langenberger calls out indistinctly*

458
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:33,600
(Henning) 'Urgent Appeal.'

459
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:38,000
'Uniting of the SPD and KPD
for this election campaign.'

460
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:40,320
*Langenberger whistles*
Let's move, colleague.

461
00:27:42,840 --> 00:27:45,320
Henning, Berlin Criminal Police. Name?

462
00:27:45,400 --> 00:27:46,400
Brock.

463
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:49,360
You are suspected of involvement

464
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:53,760
in the murder of SA man Paul Strelow
on the night of January 30th to 31st.

465
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:55,240
What, you too?

466
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:56,680
The Kripo is lending itself
to this piece-of-shit operation now?

467
00:27:57,440 --> 00:28:00,320
(Brock) You're lending yourselves to this?

468
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:03,400
You're police officers, damn it!

469
00:28:04,080 --> 00:28:05,600
You swore an oath on the constitution!

470
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:08,000
Get in there!

471
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:09,440
(Langenberger) Shut your face.
*Brock groans*

472
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:11,800
Cologne Exchange, how may I assist?

473
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:14,920
Detective Inspector Ritter,
Department A,

474
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:17,120
Berlin Police Headquarters.

475
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,520
Please connect me with Police President
Engelberth Rath.

476
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:21,720
Is this an official call?

477
00:28:22,360 --> 00:28:23,760
Yes, it is an official matter.

478
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:26,400
*phone rings*

479
00:28:27,120 --> 00:28:28,120
Yes, what is it?

480
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:33,560
Put them through.

481
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:35,160
Yes, hello,
Detective Inspector Ritter speaking.

482
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:37,760
Go ahead.

483
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:38,880
This concerns your son,
Inspector Gereon Rath.

484
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:42,320
He was last seen on January 30th
around 9 PM

485
00:28:42,760 --> 00:28:45,720
on an operation in the company
of a murder suspect.

486
00:28:45,880 --> 00:28:48,600
Since then, all trace has been lost.

487
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,120
What is your question, young lady?

488
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,800
Have you heard from him?

489
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,600
No.

490
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:02,760
Not for years.

491
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:05,040
Goodbye.

492
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:07,360
A Miss Ritter from Berlin.

493
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:13,600
(Engelberth)
She seems to miss you.

494
00:29:14,360 --> 00:29:16,360
*tense music*

495
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:18,320
*background conversation*

496
00:29:19,520 --> 00:29:21,320
Miss Ritter, for you.

497
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:41,920
For you.

498
00:29:43,360 --> 00:29:44,360
Thank you.

499
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:46,920
(Grundmann) Esteemed colleague,
Prosecutor Dresse

500
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:51,440
has apparently become Director
at the Munich Regional Court.

501
00:29:51,520 --> 00:29:54,240
Regarding the whereabouts
of the file in question,

502
00:29:54,320 --> 00:29:56,640
they declined to comment to me.

503
00:29:56,800 --> 00:29:58,880
Perhaps you will have better luck.

504
00:29:58,960 --> 00:30:00,360
Respectfully yours,
Grundmann, Army Archivist.

505
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,240
Munich Regional Court.

506
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:04,440
Berlin Police Headquarters,
Inspection A, Inspector Ritter.

507
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:07,560
I would like to speak with Director Dresse.

508
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:09,920
No, Director Dresse is no longer in office.

509
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,840
Is that so?

510
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:13,920
A week ago, he requested to be placed

511
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,000
into temporary retirement.

512
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,360
And that request was granted
with immediate effect.

513
00:30:18,440 --> 00:30:21,880
Just a week ago?

514
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,280
Yes, we are all a bit surprised,
young lady.

515
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:25,600
And...

516
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:27,640
could you perhaps give me his address?

517
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:30,680
You must apply for that in writing.

518
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:32,680
I understand.
Yes, goodbye.

519
00:30:32,760 --> 00:30:33,840
Will do. Hearing from you again.
Goodbye.

520
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:35,840
*phone rings*

521
00:30:36,600 --> 00:30:38,120
Yes?
Miss Ritter? Böhm here.

522
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:41,440
Herr Böhm?

523
00:30:41,520 --> 00:30:42,520
It may surprise you,
but we need to meet.

524
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:45,040
On official business.

525
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:46,200
Where?
At the Colonnades. Right now.

526
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:48,720
*Böhm hangs up*

527
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:50,640
Herr Böhm?

528
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:52,080
*dark music*

529
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,720
*seagulls screeching*

530
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:03,760
Why are we meeting here?

531
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:13,680
I had to ensure
our conversation remains private.

532
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:18,960
As you may have gathered,

533
00:31:19,400 --> 00:31:21,640
Political reclaimed my case.

534
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:25,080
So I heard, yes.
I'm a bit old-fashioned,

535
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:27,960
yet I will not cover up

536
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:30,680
these whitewashing operations
by Wendt and his cronies.

537
00:31:30,840 --> 00:31:33,040
What do you want from me now?

538
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:34,520
There is a connection between our two cases.

539
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:39,440
What might that be?

540
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:42,000
The dead woman in the clinic,
Sibylle Nachtwey,

541
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:45,040
and Patrolman Hoffmann

542
00:31:45,120 --> 00:31:47,000
were both strangled with a wire cord.

543
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:49,120
The identical winding of the wire,
the photographs prove it.

544
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:52,560
If there is a link between Nachtwey
and the patrolman,

545
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:56,960
then there is also one between your Dr. Forster

546
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:59,360
and the SA man Strelow.

547
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:01,040
This morning I had a witness who believes

548
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:04,760
there is a connection to yet another fatality.

549
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:07,600
We have a head start.

550
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:09,280
Political knows nothing of these ties.

551
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:11,760
Not yet.

552
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:12,840
I trust you to tell me everything
about Forster.

553
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,760
Everything that could be important to my case.

554
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:17,560
You want us to work together?

555
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:21,720
If it were up to me,
you could be working for the sanitation bureau,

556
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:26,080
or overseeing public parks in Stettin.

557
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:29,360
It just so happens that chance

558
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:31,040
washed you up into Gennat's Homicide Division
at Alexanderplatz.

559
00:32:31,120 --> 00:32:34,520
And that you, much as I hoped
to be rid of you...

560
00:32:34,600 --> 00:32:37,600
How do I know I can rely on you?

561
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:40,200
I laid out everything I know.

562
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:43,080
If it leaks out that I'm continuing to investigate,

563
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:44,840
I'm finished.

564
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,000
That's why I need your help.

565
00:32:47,320 --> 00:32:49,240
Fine.

566
00:32:53,080 --> 00:32:54,080
I'll check out Strelow's duty stations.

567
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:57,880
I'll get a car
and take a look around his circle.

568
00:32:58,040 --> 00:33:00,840
*dynamic string music*

569
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:02,680
*murmuring*

570
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:09,560
*ominous music*

571
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:11,840
Comrade.

572
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:20,040
Is this the KPD headquarters?

573
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,600
District headquarters, yes.

574
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:25,920
I need to meet leadership.

575
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:28,240
Who's that?
- Völcker, she's inside.

576
00:33:28,400 --> 00:33:31,320
Take me to her right now, please.

577
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,400
What's wrong with your eye?

578
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:36,280
I was a bricklayer.

579
00:33:36,440 --> 00:33:38,160
Got slaked lime in my eye.

580
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:40,640
Comrades, I have traveled
all the way from Holland

581
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:45,680
to bring you an important message.

582
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:48,600
We must stop talking, we must act.

583
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:52,520
In action lies our hope.

584
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:55,080
Capitalism cannot be fought

585
00:33:55,840 --> 00:33:57,440
in the shadow of fascism.

586
00:33:57,600 --> 00:34:00,080
Comrade, who sent you?

587
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:02,240
I am a messenger from the CPH Leiden,
South Holland,

588
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:06,320
self-appointed, and my message is:

589
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:08,960
together we must send a signal.

590
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:11,520
The enemy wants to rule in Berlin.

591
00:34:11,679 --> 00:34:14,600
Let us attack the bigwigs.

592
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:16,480
Let us destroy the parliaments.
Burn them to the ground.

593
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,800
Excuse me,
we have work to do here.

594
00:34:19,880 --> 00:34:22,320
I haven't finished...
There is...

595
00:34:23,920 --> 00:34:26,760
Alright, out you go.
- Let go of me.

596
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,880
Easy now.
- (van der Lubbe) Let go!

597
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:31,960
(Man) Fresh air will do you good.

598
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:34,080
(van der Lubbe) Let go of me!

599
00:34:34,679 --> 00:34:36,239
Right, now beat it.

600
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,800
You will talk, talk, talk,

601
00:34:45,120 --> 00:34:47,520
and then suddenly... too late!

602
00:34:47,679 --> 00:34:50,000
Action! Action!

603
00:34:50,679 --> 00:34:53,199
That is what we must take!

604
00:34:54,719 --> 00:34:56,040
(Albrecht)
Your thoughts are sound, comrade!

605
00:34:56,679 --> 00:34:58,880
Those folks just don't understand.

606
00:35:09,720 --> 00:35:11,800
Come with me.

607
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:15,240
Where to?

608
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,080
I'll buy you a meal, a warm one.

609
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:21,800
Come on.

610
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:23,760
*somber music*

611
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:28,680
*bird cawing*

612
00:35:30,640 --> 00:35:32,680
*she sighs*

613
00:35:35,120 --> 00:35:37,360
*chaotic cawing*

614
00:35:48,280 --> 00:35:50,080
Frau Strelow?

615
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,440
Good day. Gerlinde Sturm,
NSDAP Bereavement Care.

616
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:12,960
Do you have a moment for me?
(Berlin dialect) Nope.

617
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:16,240
Your party has his death on its conscience.

618
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:28,560
Now you want to turn him into a hero

619
00:36:28,640 --> 00:36:30,520
with your state hullabaloo.

620
00:36:30,600 --> 00:36:32,360
*music fades out*

621
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:33,880
*chickens clucking*

622
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,240
(Berlin dialect) If that's how it is,

623
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:38,120
I can talk straight with you.

624
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,400
The Nazis can kiss my backside.

625
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:43,480
I'm here because my fiancé is missing.

626
00:36:43,560 --> 00:36:45,520
And the last person

627
00:36:46,320 --> 00:36:47,320
who asked after him was your son.

628
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:49,800
I haven't seen my son in years.

629
00:36:52,040 --> 00:36:54,280
*dog barking*

630
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,160
That's him, engagement photos.

631
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:02,720
His name is Gereon. Gereon Rath.

632
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,760
You're Gereon's fiancée?

633
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,600
You know him?

634
00:37:11,880 --> 00:37:12,880
Certainly do.
He was just here the other day.

635
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:17,160
Picked something up for my son.

636
00:37:18,280 --> 00:37:20,480
And when was that?

637
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:22,440
Well, when that loudmouth
became Chancellor.

638
00:37:23,200 --> 00:37:25,880
I remember that day well.

639
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:29,040
Only what he picked up, I don't know.

640
00:37:30,560 --> 00:37:32,680
I do.

641
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:35,880
Explosives. In a cognac box.

642
00:37:37,240 --> 00:37:39,960
Why didn't you say right away
that you knew?

643
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:45,360
*threatening music*

644
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:47,120
Well, you'd better keep a close eye
on your Gereon.

645
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:50,000
Lest something happens to him too.

646
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,640
He was a demolition man,
my son.

647
00:37:53,960 --> 00:37:56,600
And what does Gereon have to do with this?

648
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:11,640
I thought you knew?

649
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:15,520
No, not about that.

650
00:38:16,960 --> 00:38:19,520
And what is it for?

651
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,240
How should I know?

652
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:26,400
Now get out of here!

653
00:38:29,200 --> 00:38:30,520
*bells tolling*

654
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:38,960
*sigh*

655
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:52,120
Good day, Frau Strelow.

656
00:38:56,920 --> 00:38:58,480
Come on.

657
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:01,440
*music fades out*

658
00:39:02,360 --> 00:39:03,520
*traffic noise*

659
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:05,640
Herr Heymann didn't happen
to leave a message?

660
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:18,000
No, not with me.

661
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,560
And how did your two party leaders
react, then?

662
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:23,280
With Ernst Thälmann, it took forever
before they let me in.

663
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:26,960
I hadn't even outlined my idea
before he cut me off.

664
00:39:27,120 --> 00:39:29,880
Please, hear me out.
- They are born traitors.

665
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:33,600
I said 'no'!

666
00:39:33,680 --> 00:39:35,480
(Litten) Deaf ears.

667
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:37,320
And on your end?

668
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:39,560
Similar.

669
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:41,440
Thälmann just wants to make a fool of me.

670
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:43,640
I held out my hand, nothing came back.

671
00:39:43,720 --> 00:39:45,920
Deputy Wels...
- Oh, spare me.

672
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:48,360
The resentment runs too deep.

673
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:51,040
These top dogs don't trust each other,
and their parties even less.

674
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:54,520
Nobody grasps the gravity of the situation.

675
00:39:54,680 --> 00:39:56,600
Frau Elisabeth, this soup of yours
is pure comfort food.

676
00:39:58,640 --> 00:40:02,160
(Litten) Outstanding.

677
00:40:03,520 --> 00:40:04,680
So, if I understood you correctly,

678
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:07,200
an electoral alliance between the two leftist parties

679
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:11,280
is the last chance to prevent Hitler in the election.

680
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:15,040
Correct.
- Yes.

681
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:16,240
Yet the chairmen of both parties

682
00:40:16,320 --> 00:40:18,320
insist on past positions,

683
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:21,400
failing to recognize
that they must swallow their pride.

684
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:24,160
Correct.
- Yes.

685
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:25,240
Then you must speak with other people
in the parties.

686
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:29,000
With whom?
- With whom?

687
00:40:29,160 --> 00:40:30,360
With the women.

688
00:40:30,520 --> 00:40:31,720
Herr Katelbach.
- What?

689
00:40:37,400 --> 00:40:39,560
Cross your heart now, Frau Behnke.

690
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:41,720
Women?
- Women, yes.

691
00:40:42,760 --> 00:40:44,880
Who else would be capable,

692
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,280
beyond the shadows of the past,

693
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:49,200
of keeping a clear eye on the future?

694
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:51,440
Or was it because of you two
that you were turned away so abruptly?

695
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:54,920
Us?
- No, not in the least...

696
00:40:55,080 --> 00:40:56,640
Who could such a woman be?

697
00:40:56,720 --> 00:40:58,680
One respected by Communists
and Social Democrats alike?

698
00:40:58,840 --> 00:41:02,800
The ideal figure of a united left?

699
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:06,360
*she nods*

700
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,440
A Social Democratic Communist?

701
00:41:07,520 --> 00:41:09,840
Or a Communist Social Democrat?

702
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,040
Like Tussy Marx. Karl's daughter.

703
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:14,200
Not bad: 'Red Nobility', a good start.

704
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:17,080
Only trouble is, Tussy is dead.

705
00:41:17,240 --> 00:41:19,040
Something like that, though.
Young, but not too young.

706
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:21,400
With a certain intellectual allure.

707
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:24,920
Yes, austere yet approachable.
- Moderate, yet radical all the same.

708
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:28,680
Yes, yes, yes.

709
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:29,840
I propose: a Luxemburg in the flesh.

710
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:32,880
Clara Luxemburg.
- Never heard of her.

711
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:35,560
Does she exist?
- No. But she could.

712
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:38,440
The long-lost sister.

713
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:40,160
The youngest of the five Luxemburg children.

714
00:41:40,240 --> 00:41:42,680
Oh no. My God. The baby of the family.

715
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:45,320
Straight out of charming Zamość.

716
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:47,240
Clara.

717
00:41:47,320 --> 00:41:48,320
She could pull it off. No one else.

718
00:41:48,480 --> 00:41:50,200
*cheerful laughter*

719
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:51,440
*Katelbach clears throat and huffs*

720
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:55,320
Clara Luxemburg it is, then.

721
00:41:58,600 --> 00:42:00,560
*boisterous piano music*

722
00:42:00,720 --> 00:42:02,560
(Doris)
I was in a dance marathon once.

723
00:42:04,600 --> 00:42:06,400
Collapsed right before the end.

724
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:08,400
Next year I want to compete again.
Care to join?

725
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:11,280
Anyone can dance.

726
00:42:11,800 --> 00:42:13,120
Not with two left feet.
- Let me see.

727
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:15,760
Hopeless case with me.

728
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:18,000
It'll work out. I'll manage.

729
00:42:21,480 --> 00:42:23,600
If you... if you say so.

730
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:26,920
I do.

731
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:28,720
Well, otherwise we can just go to the movies?

732
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:36,120
What kind of person are you...

733
00:42:39,280 --> 00:42:40,600
What kind of guy are you, anyway?

734
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:42,760
What do you mean?

735
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,440
I need to know before we go to the movies.

736
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:46,600
That's usually just the beginning
of something, isn't it?

737
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:49,080
What can I say?

738
00:42:49,520 --> 00:42:50,520
Ex-Communist trying

739
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:52,720
to remain a good person in wicked times.

740
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,960
A good start.

741
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:56,960
The ex-Communist?
- The halfway decent person.

742
00:42:57,120 --> 00:42:59,760
Go on.

743
00:43:01,160 --> 00:43:02,160
No, your turn.

744
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:03,760
I am a socialist as well.

745
00:43:04,200 --> 00:43:06,200
Really?
- Yes. A National Socialist.

746
00:43:06,280 --> 00:43:08,480
Oh.

747
00:43:09,440 --> 00:43:10,640
Don't worry. We both want the same thing.

748
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:13,160
I don't think so.

749
00:43:13,720 --> 00:43:14,840
Sure, for the working man
to have a voice again.

750
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:18,440
Hm.

751
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:21,000
Come on, what do you want to know?

752
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:23,600
You know how to dance.

753
00:43:25,560 --> 00:43:26,920
You're politically unsteady.

754
00:43:27,760 --> 00:43:30,080
Overall, very kind.

755
00:43:30,600 --> 00:43:32,720
Overall, very kind.

756
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:34,680
And very handsome, too.

757
00:43:34,840 --> 00:43:36,720
Those aren't questions.

758
00:43:36,800 --> 00:43:37,800
You're right.

759
00:43:39,200 --> 00:43:41,040
I just can't think of any question.

760
00:43:41,800 --> 00:43:43,680
*romantic music*

761
00:43:53,320 --> 00:43:55,280
*music fades out*

762
00:43:55,360 --> 00:43:57,280
*background chatter*

763
00:43:59,440 --> 00:44:01,680
*laughter, cheerful dance music*

764
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:04,200
Well, to what do I owe the honor?

765
00:44:05,760 --> 00:44:07,360
Your old inspector?

766
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:09,440
Has he still not surfaced?

767
00:44:09,520 --> 00:44:12,760
Has he once again told nothing
but the complete untruth?

768
00:44:12,840 --> 00:44:13,840
Indeed.

769
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:16,520
Thank you.

770
00:44:17,840 --> 00:44:19,480
You keep falling for the washouts.

771
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:21,840
The good ones always fall
for the washouts. Every time.

772
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:24,880
Nature intended it that way.

773
00:44:25,040 --> 00:44:27,200
What do you know of nature?
More than you, my friend.

774
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:28,280
*man laughs*

775
00:44:28,440 --> 00:44:30,920
Mark my words, one fine day you'll think:

776
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:32,000
Old Jacky...

777
00:44:32,160 --> 00:44:33,600
*Jacky sighs contentedly*

778
00:44:34,040 --> 00:44:35,600
...he would have been the one.

779
00:44:37,520 --> 00:44:40,120
Yes, but by then? By then it's too late.

780
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:43,240
And what is that supposed to mean?

781
00:44:44,680 --> 00:44:46,000
Glad you're here.

782
00:44:47,160 --> 00:44:48,600
*door chime rings*

783
00:44:50,120 --> 00:44:53,080
Reinhold. I was hoping you'd be here.

784
00:44:54,200 --> 00:44:55,200
You know me.

785
00:44:56,520 --> 00:44:57,920
Jacky.
- Good evening.

786
00:44:59,320 --> 00:45:00,640
I wanted to say thank you.

787
00:45:03,320 --> 00:45:04,320
Dance?

788
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:06,160
Sure thing.

789
00:45:07,760 --> 00:45:11,680
'Rosa Luxemburg was conscious
of her Polish-Jewish heritage,

790
00:45:11,760 --> 00:45:14,280
yet refused to be reduced to it.'

791
00:45:14,360 --> 00:45:15,760
(whispers) Reduced...

792
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:19,080
'Her struggle was full of passion,
politically and personally.

793
00:45:19,160 --> 00:45:21,240
A modern woman and a lover,

794
00:45:21,320 --> 00:45:23,720
who courageously accepted the risk of failure.

795
00:45:24,640 --> 00:45:28,120
She always made her political convictions
the benchmark...'

796
00:45:28,200 --> 00:45:29,480
Are you still awake?

797
00:45:30,160 --> 00:45:32,920
Sorry, did I wake you?
- No.

798
00:45:35,760 --> 00:45:37,920
Can't sleep anyway.

799
00:45:41,440 --> 00:45:44,160
After everything that's happened
these past few days,

800
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:45,920
I see dark times ahead.

801
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:56,080
Maybe we should pack our bags
and head to Vienna.

802
00:45:58,680 --> 00:46:00,320
What would I do in Vienna?

803
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:03,600
Well, it's my hometown, after all.

804
00:46:03,680 --> 00:46:05,960
Half my relatives are there.

805
00:46:06,040 --> 00:46:09,320
It has the world's largest cemetery, too.
Nothing but advantages.

806
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:11,000
And then?

807
00:46:14,760 --> 00:46:15,760
Then...

808
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:18,440
we get married there.

809
00:46:21,080 --> 00:46:22,760
Like I said: nothing but advantages.

810
00:46:23,480 --> 00:46:25,720
You'll get an Austrian passport.

811
00:46:25,800 --> 00:46:28,920
And if things get worse here,
we'll take a trip.

812
00:46:30,680 --> 00:46:32,120
Where to?
- Mhm.

813
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:35,440
Wherever you want, Elisabeth,
I'll follow you.

814
00:46:36,360 --> 00:46:38,840
Prague, Rome, London,

815
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:41,360
Budapest.
- Zanzibar?

816
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:43,680
Zanzibar?

817
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:46,400
What would we do there?

818
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:48,160
On the radio, they say

819
00:46:48,320 --> 00:46:50,800
you can swim in the ocean like in a bathtub.

820
00:46:50,880 --> 00:46:52,440
Swim in the ocean?

821
00:46:53,600 --> 00:46:55,800
I'm a Jew, I sit in coffeehouses.

822
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:58,280
He doesn't swim in the ocean.
Fish swim in the ocean.

823
00:46:58,920 --> 00:47:01,080
Or does the fish sit in a coffeehouse?

824
00:47:01,760 --> 00:47:04,000
And what will we live on?

825
00:47:04,480 --> 00:47:06,680
Well, I'll write about our travels.

826
00:47:08,080 --> 00:47:09,760
Just like that, it's possible?

827
00:47:09,840 --> 00:47:13,080
Egon Kisch does the exact same thing
and makes a good living from it.

828
00:47:13,520 --> 00:47:18,200
One simply has to observe the world
with an alert mind and sharp eyes.

829
00:47:40,200 --> 00:47:42,400
*"Je rêve" by Zaho de Sagazan*

830
00:47:42,480 --> 00:47:44,720
*melancholy ballad in French*

831
00:47:48,920 --> 00:47:55,880
# I close my eyes, imagining the two of us #

832
00:47:56,560 --> 00:48:02,520
# Intertwined, lips dried by love #

833
00:48:02,600 --> 00:48:04,640
# Love for each other #

834
00:48:05,680 --> 00:48:13,320
# I dream, I dream, mmm, I dream, oh yes, I dream #

835
00:48:14,240 --> 00:48:17,440
# I turn over our memories in my mind #

836
00:48:17,880 --> 00:48:22,160
# That time desperately tries to destroy #

837
00:48:22,720 --> 00:48:26,720
# A smile and tears slip into the corners of my eyes #

838
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:30,840
# How to imagine the future, heal from yesterday #

839
00:48:30,920 --> 00:48:39,480
# Oh, I dream, mmm, I dream, oh yes, I dream #

840
00:48:39,880 --> 00:48:46,440
# I dream, I dream, I dream #

841
00:48:47,440 --> 00:48:53,760
# That you are here with me #

842
00:48:56,960 --> 00:49:03,320
# I dream, oh yes, I dream, I dream #

843
00:49:04,320 --> 00:49:12,000
# But you are not, no, no, you're not really here #

844
00:49:14,880 --> 00:49:16,880
*music softens gently*

845
00:49:18,560 --> 00:49:23,640
# I feel my heart stopping in my chest #

846
00:49:23,720 --> 00:49:26,040
# I dream and pretend #

847
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:30,800
# Not to have felt this reality pass by #

848
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:35,680
# That you will stay asleep, but never again by my side #

849
00:49:35,760 --> 00:49:43,320
# I dream, mmm, I dream, ah, I dream, oh yes, I dream #

850
00:49:44,200 --> 00:49:48,160
# All I do is dream, imagine what you might have become #

851
00:49:48,320 --> 00:49:52,600
# If only they had left you the time to build it #

852
00:49:52,680 --> 00:49:54,520
# I loved loving you so much #

853
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:57,160
# I will never cease to do so, for death #

854
00:49:57,240 --> 00:50:01,040
# Does not stop one from dreaming, so I close my eyes again #

855
00:50:01,120 --> 00:50:02,800
# And I dream #

856
00:50:03,520 --> 00:50:08,000
# I dream, I dream #

857
00:50:08,920 --> 00:50:15,480
# That you are here with me #

858
00:50:17,560 --> 00:50:22,240
# I dream, oh-oh-oh... #

859
00:50:26,480 --> 00:50:28,160
*music slows down*

860
00:50:29,840 --> 00:50:31,240
*loud snoring*

861
00:50:36,120 --> 00:50:37,120
Herr Böhm?

862
00:50:41,920 --> 00:50:43,280
*music ends*

863
00:50:44,160 --> 00:50:45,160
Whoops.

864
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:47,120
*she huffs embarrassedly*

865
00:50:47,720 --> 00:50:49,000
Finally.

866
00:50:49,920 --> 00:50:51,960
Thought you weren't coming anymore.

867
00:50:52,520 --> 00:50:54,000
What are you doing here?

868
00:50:55,000 --> 00:50:57,080
I was at Strelow's last workplace.

869
00:50:57,840 --> 00:50:59,400
Should interest you.

870
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:01,480
Come along. Personally, too.

871
00:51:02,240 --> 00:51:03,440
*phone rings*

872
00:51:04,600 --> 00:51:05,600
Yes, hello?

873
00:51:06,200 --> 00:51:07,200
Hello.

874
00:51:11,880 --> 00:51:12,880
Damn it.

875
00:51:13,480 --> 00:51:14,480
What happened?

876
00:51:17,080 --> 00:51:19,440
I thought...
- Heard nothing yet?

877
00:51:21,840 --> 00:51:24,280
I need electricity and a wall.

878
00:51:24,440 --> 00:51:25,800
*projector flickers*

879
00:51:25,880 --> 00:51:28,640
I got this from the Institute
for Suggestive Therapy.

880
00:51:29,880 --> 00:51:32,160
Apparently Strelow's last workplace.

881
00:51:34,120 --> 00:51:35,120
That one there.

882
00:51:35,840 --> 00:51:37,920
He came to see me today,
Franz Krajewski.

883
00:51:40,240 --> 00:51:42,040
And that one there, that's Strelow.

884
00:51:44,840 --> 00:51:47,440
Spent years in this institute.

885
00:51:47,520 --> 00:51:50,240
First as a patient,
later as a caretaker.

886
00:51:50,320 --> 00:51:51,800
Then he joined the SA.

887
00:51:51,960 --> 00:51:53,360
Just wait, though.

888
00:51:54,520 --> 00:51:55,520
Now.

889
00:51:58,040 --> 00:51:59,840
*somber pulsing music*

890
00:52:03,400 --> 00:52:04,600
Gereon.

891
00:52:07,040 --> 00:52:10,280
I seized the film right away.

892
00:52:14,320 --> 00:52:15,720
Where is this institute?

893
00:52:16,840 --> 00:52:18,000
Way out in the sticks.

894
00:52:19,680 --> 00:52:21,600
Out in Johannisthal.

895
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:34,360
And who is that?

896
00:52:35,720 --> 00:52:37,160
*Böhm snores*

897
00:52:42,520 --> 00:52:44,840
*music builds suspensefully*

898
00:53:09,560 --> 00:53:11,640
*eerie music*

899
00:53:23,040 --> 00:53:24,360
(Man) Come in.

900
00:53:28,560 --> 00:53:29,840
*music subsides*

901
00:53:36,720 --> 00:53:38,040
*door closes*

902
00:53:38,960 --> 00:53:41,600
*music turns more suspenseful*

903
00:53:54,480 --> 00:53:57,600
Take a seat, Miss Ritter.

904
00:53:59,000 --> 00:54:00,000
*

